  "term": "exon",
  "definition": "An exon is a segment of a eukaryotic gene’s RNA transcript that is kept and joined with other retained segments during RNA splicing after introns are removed. Different ways of combining exons through alternative splicing help create diversity in gene transcripts and the proteins they can produce.",
